{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED at exact head 93111cf97d95e8082730c398d87ad80492f3d394.\n\nArchitecture: affected layers are 4 (application host binding), 5 (application profile/interpreter), and 6 (internal/app host and boundary adapter); the kernel stays unchanged, and the architecture page is updated at this head. The binding scan, latest-authorized-binding rule, malformed/unauthorized no-force rule, checkpoint profile separation, and removal of the false Workroom-typed registry are coherent. One exact contract condition is nevertheless not met: the ratified design, architecture page, original request 5682b414, and repair request fbd59f32 all require read-binding/select-interpreter once at open. OpenObserved deliberately defers selection until first fold or append. A focused review regression opened a workspace, appended a replacement binding through another workspace, then first selected from the already-open workspace; it observed the later binding and failed with uninterpretable instead of retaining the binding at open. Selection timing is therefore dependent on activity after Open. Move selection to the open boundary, or obtain and document a ratified contract change; add a regression that pins the chosen semantics.\n\nSecurity: the actor-signature, target, payload-tree, canonical JSON, ceiling, and initializing-key checks are sound, and no untrusted application code is loaded or run. There is one unresolved failure-mode defect. snapshotWithSource calls interpreter before the kernel reader audit, and interpreter returns a definitive error saying the repository is verifiable but uninterpretable. A focused review regression took a valid initializer-signed binding request, placed it in a commit signed by the wrong sequencer key, advanced the ref, and called Snapshot. The exact head returned verifiable-but-uninterpretable before the kernel could report the invalid sequencer signature. Thus an untrusted Git history can mask an unverifiable chain as an interpreter refusal. Preserve read-binding/select-before-fold, but do not return a verifiability claim or interpreter refusal ahead of kernel verification; add a regression requiring the sequencer-signature failure to win. Audit the analogous AcceptSubmission order as part of the fix.\n\nSimplification: removing the one-entry map and exported kernel.ReadOpening is a real simplification. The lazy atomic selection state is not: it adds a timing-dependent path contrary to the governing open-time contract. Resolving and caching the selection at Open makes the boundary simpler and deterministic. No other cut is required.\n\nEvidence: both candidate artifacts were live and non-stale; current main moved only README.md and merge-tree was clean. git diff --check passed. Existing focused gates passed at this exact head: go test ./internal/app ./internal/docset/... -count=1 (app 200.856s, docset 245.231s). The two review-only regressions above both failed in the stated way. Do not merge this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ac7663413e45233605bb59b03fcac540ef02ea9a","head":"93111cf97d95e8082730c398d87ad80492f3d394","verdict":"changes-requested"}}